skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how proveo runs a harness unattended at set times — a minutely tick, a tmux terminal, a typed goal
' covers: internal/schedule/schedule.go
' covers: internal/schedule/runner.go
' covers: internal/schedule/install.go
' covers: internal/schedule/install_test.go
' covers: internal/schedule/schedule_test.go
' covers: internal/schedule/table.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/schedule.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/schedule_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/running.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/running_test.go
' covers: e2e/schedule_test.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go (resolveAddonFlags), internal/run/params.go (AddonsSet, Yes)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/stop_signal_test.go
'   the Glimmer early stop this works around ... _spec/_experiments/sbx-host-inference.puml
'
' ── WHY NOT A PLAIN CRON (2026-09-27) ──────────────────────────────────────
' Every harness is a TUI. cron/launchd give no TTY, so proveo's choice form,
' hermes's TUI and `/goal` are unreachable. Measured: `hermes chat -q "/goal …"`
' on a TTY QUEUES the text as a user message; on a non-TTY it is --oneshot, one
' turn and exit, and hermes runs goal loops in -q only for kanban workers. So
' the goal has to be TYPED into the running TUI — which needs a terminal proveo
' owns. internal/tmux already drives TUIs for the e2e suite.
'
' ── SHAPE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   launchd (macOS) / systemd --user timer (Linux) → `proveo schedule tick` every 60 s
'   tick   stateless: load ~/.proveo/schedule.yml + schedule-state.json; for each job
'          whose newest `at` entry fell within catch_up (20 m) and has not fired:
'          mark it fired, then Launch
'   Launch tmux session proveo-sched-<job> running `PROVEO_SCHEDULE=1 proveo run
'          <target> --yes --local-model … --addon …` (or the job's `command`),
'          pipe-pane to
'          ~/.proveo/logs/schedule/<job>/<stamp>.log, and a detached (setsid)
'          `proveo schedule watch`
'   watch  caffeinate -i (macOS); wait ≤10 m for the ready marker (default ❯),
'          then for the pane to hold still 3 s (≤60 s); type the prompt file
'          flattened to one line as `/goal …` (or /loop, or plain) + Enter;
'          wait ≤30 s for the accepted marker, retype up to 3 tries;
'          at the budget type /exit, then kill after 90 s;
'          write <stamp>.json {outcome: ended|budget|not-ready|failed} and notify
' One session per job: a tick that finds the session still up skips it.
'
' ── WHAT THE LISTING PRINTS (2026-11-11, R4 of _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml)
' `proveo schedule` (or `ls`) draws no heading: ONE ui.Facts block keyed by job,
' scheduler role, soonest first, then a × item per failed job, then ONE closing
' line for the tick, printed last:
'   ● waivers: running since 20:37 EDT · 23m of 1h
'              Tue Sep 29 20:00 EDT · in 1d 23h
'                hermes · goal · 1h budget
'   ● lineup:  Thu Oct 1 18:50 EDT · in 3d 21h
'              Sun Oct 4 11:35 EDT · in 6d 14h
'                hermes · muse-glimmer:30b-mlx · goal · 45m budget
'   ● probe:   manual
'              command · plain · 45m budget
'   × lineup — failed Sun Sep 27 11:35
'       the agent exited 4 before it was ready: …
'       ~/.proveo/logs/schedule/lineup/20260927-113500.log
'       `proveo schedule retry lineup` runs it again
'   ✓ tick — installed
'       launchd io.proveo.schedule, every 60s
' The value is the soonest run "<Mon Jan 2 15:04 MST> · in <wait>", or the
' running value; each later run stacks under it (P3, the operator's "stack each
' run"); the job's target · model · mode · budget and "last <when> <outcome>
' [· <summary>]" sit dim two columns past the last stacked value, or under the
' value when nothing stacks. A failed job's × says its last run, so no "last"
' line repeats it. "idle", "-", "last never", ▸, the entry column ("mon 18:50")
' and the transcripts row are gone (P8, P9); the transcripts folder is in
' `proveo schedule --help`.
' A job with no `at` lists as "manual" (Rows gives it one row with a zero Next,
' sorted last), so a schedule of `schedule run` jobs is not read as empty, its
' failure shows, and `proveo attach` lists it while it runs.
' THE RUNNING VALUE is one line, the same in this listing, in `proveo attach`'s
' list and (behind a "● ") in the attach and run pickers (RunningTask.Value,
' .Summary): "running since <start, job tz> · <elapsed> of <budget>[, past the
' budget]", or "running now" when no transcript names the start; elapsed and
' budget in the budget's own form ("1h7m of 1h30m", as "1h30m budget" below
' it), while waits read ui.Span ("in 1d 23h"). start = the
' stamp of the newest <stamp>.log without <stamp>.exit (CurrentRun). It is the
' job's VALUE, the first thing after its name: 2026-10-04 a live
' muse-lineup-refine showed only the word "running" mid-line, beside a "last …
' done" from Oct 1, and read as idle; position, not a caller colour, fixes it.
' THE TICK LINE (one state reads one way here and in `schedule install`):
'   ✓ tick — installed            dim the manager ("launchd io.proveo.schedule,
'                                 every 60s" / "systemd --user …, every minute")
'   ⚠ tick — its last run exited N    dim the log `launchctl print` names
'   ⚠ tick — reads ~/.proveo/schedule.yml, not this home's   (no how-to)
'   ⚠ tick — not installed        dim "`proveo schedule install` registers it
'                                 with launchd" — only when a job has a set time
'                                 and that tick would read this home (another
'                                 PROVEO_HOME: no how-to; Tick.Home names
'                                 ~/.proveo installed or not)
'   ● tick — not installed        nothing would fire: no jobs, or manual ones
'   ⚠/● tick — no service manager on <os>   dim "run `proveo schedule tick`
'                                 every minute yourself", not on windows (no
'                                 tmux, no sh)
' NOTHING TO LIST. No schedule.yml prints "● no ~/.proveo/schedule.yml" and an
' empty one "● no jobs in <~file>"; then every line, the tick's too, goes to
' stderr and stdout stays empty (_spec/cmd/proveo/usage.puml). Both exit 0, and
' the tick with no schedule.yml finds nothing due, logs nothing and exits 0, so
' a ⚠ "last run exited N" always means a real failure (the operator, "both exit
' 0"). An invalid file is "× <~file> — not valid" with the reason dim, exit 1.
' A stray argument to schedule, ls, tick, install or uninstall is ignored and
' a mistyped subcommand lists, as at HEAD: R4 changes no argument rule.
' covers: internal/schedule/table.go, internal/schedule/table_test.go
' Times are wall-clock in the job's tz, so DST keeps "sun 11:35" at 11:35.
'
' ── FAILURE + RETRY (2026-09-28) ───────────────────────────────────────────
' failed ≡ outcome ∈ {failed, not-ready}. Three sources feed it:
'   launch   tick's Launch errors → RecordLaunchFailure writes <stamp>.json
'            {outcome: failed, detail: "launch: …"}; ErrRunning (session still
'            up) is a skip, not a failure
'   exit     the session runs `cd <wd> && <argv>; echo $? > <stamp>.exit` (no
'            exec, so sh outlives the agent); an early end with status ≠ 0 is
'            failed "the agent exited N before the budget", 0 stays ended
'   watch    prompt unreadable, ready marker absent (not-ready), send-keys error
' `proveo schedule` prints "× <job> — <outcome> <started, job tz>" after the
' block while the job is idle (a running job hides it), its detail's first line
' and its transcript dim. Its retry how-to prints dim only when no question
' can follow (a pipe; the NO TTY rule): on a TTY (stdin ∧ stdout) the question
' "retry <job>? [y/N]" takes that line's place, and the relaunch's ✓ or ×
' follows it, so the tick line still prints last (R3's "a closing verdict
' prints last, once"). A refused relaunch prints its × and the next question
' still comes; the listing then exits 1. Tick and pipes never prompt.
' `proveo schedule retry <job>` relaunches under the failed run's entry and
' prints "✓ <job> — started again"; `run` prints "✓ <job> — started". Every
' refusal is one × item with ONE dim line, printed by the command, Reported
' (exit 1, main adds nothing; cmd/proveo/schedule.go refuse):
'   × <job> — has not run yet           `proveo schedule run <job>` starts it now
'   × <job> — its last run did not fail `proveo schedule run <job>` starts it again
'   × <job> — no such job               jobs: <names>
'   × <job> — already running           `proveo attach <job>` opens it
'   × <job> — its tmux session did not start   tmux's own words (tmux.Session.Start)
'   × <job> — not started               any other launch error, home paths as ~/
'   × <~file> — not found               `proveo schedule --help` shows its format
' The tick log names a skipped job once: "… tick: <job> (<entry>): still
' running (tmux session proveo-sched-<job>)" (ErrRunning carries no name).
' No auto-retry: a failed run waits for its next `at` or an operator.
'
' ── READY ≠ TAKING INPUT (2026-09-28, first real hermes run) ────────────────
' hermes draws `❯ Find and fix a failing test` (its placeholder) while agent
' init still blocks the TUI: the typed goal rendered with dropped characters
' and Enter cleared it without a turn (agent.log: no turn, `ollama ps`: empty).
' Hand-retyping the same line 4 min later started the goal. Two guards:
'   settle    marker seen ∧ pane unchanged for settleQuiet
'   accepted  job `accepted:` › defaultAccepted[target+" "+mode]
'             ({"hermes goal": "Goal (active"}) › first 24 runes of the prompt
'             (echoed by most TUIs as the user turn). Residual: a lost Enter
'             leaves the text in the input box, which also matches.
' The same run's first attempt also exposed WaitFor polling a dead pane for
' 10 m: every wait now checks has-session and ends with
' "the agent exited N before it was ready: <last 3 transcript lines>".
'
' ── REPORT (2026-09-28) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' An outcome says how the run ENDED, never what it DID: the first real run
' spent 38 min asking "confirm Week 4?" and recorded `budget`, same as a run
' that set a lineup. The agent's own words are the only witness, and every
' harness can write a file, so the contract is a file, not a harness adapter:
'   prompt asks for <workdir>/report.md, first line "RESULT: <verdict>"
'   Watch removes a stale report.md before typing; finish moves it to
'   <stamp>.report.md and sets result.summary (RESULT line, else first line)
'   and result.report (path). The listing appends "· <summary>", or
'   "· no report" for ended/budget, to the job's `last`.
' HANDOFF ≠ REPORT: report.md is for the manager and moves to the logs;
' <workdir>/<task>.md is what the NEXT task needs as input, written by the
' agent (skill `scheduled-run`), never touched by the watcher. The logs
' folder is not mounted in the sandbox, so a second task that shares the
' workdir (lineup pass 2) reads pass 1's handoff there, checking its week
' and time so a stale one from an earlier week is ignored.
' <workdir> is ~/.proveo/schedule/<task> unless `workdir:`; proveo run mounts
' it rw at the same path, so the prompt names the host path verbatim.
' EARLY EXIT: `/goal` ending does not end the TUI — hermes idles at its
' prompt until the budget. So a report IS the finish line: once report.md is
' non-empty, Watch waits for the pane to hold still doneQuiet (20 s, ≤3 m —
' the agent echoes the report), then runs the budget-stop ladder and records
' outcome `done` "report written after Nm; stopped early with /exit".
' Residual: a draft report written mid-run ends the run ≤3 m later.
' Edits to schedule.yml and prompt files take effect on the next tick / run:
' tick and watch reload both each time; `install` only registers the tick.
'
' SUBMIT: typing "/goal …" opens hermes's slash-command menu, which can take
' the ⏎ as "accept completion" (rehearsal 2: the goal sat typed-but-unsent
' for 4 min, the ❯ marker vanished and attempt 3 waited on it). After ⏎
' the watcher waits submitWait (5 s) for the accepted marker and presses ⏎
' once more before it would ever retype. `schedule watch --typed` (Rewatch)
' takes over a run whose instruction is already in: report or budget only.

' ── BUDGET STOP (2026-09-28) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' The first real run typed /exit into a BUSY hermes (no effect), was killed at
' +90 s, and the kill orphaned its sandbox: SIGHUP took proveo down before its
' deferred teardown, and the agent made browser calls for 24 s with no
' terminal. The stop is now a ladder, gentlest first:
'   C-c (interrupt the turn) · 5 s · /exit ⏎ · 5 s · ⏎ again · ≤90 s
'   (rehearsal 2026-09-28: hermes's slash-command menu took the first ⏎ as
'   "accept completion"; /exit sat unsubmitted until SIGTERM)
'   SIGTERM every child of the pane's sh (= `proveo run`) · ≤60 s
'   tmux kill-session
' `proveo run` on sbx turns SIGTERM/SIGHUP into a cancelled context: the sbx
' client gets SIGTERM (WaitDelay 30 s) and the deferred teardown runs, so a
' closed terminal or a kill-session no longer leaks a running sandbox.
' Since 2026-10-17 (the user: "Stop runs normal teardown") that teardown is
' the NORMAL-EXIT one: the clone and state are lifted home and `sbx rm` runs —
' what this ladder's SIGTERM rung expected all along (internal/schedule/
' runner.go:440: "SIGTERM the pane's command so `proveo run` tears its sandbox
' down"). The same day the user chose "Exit 128+sig, 'stopped' (Recommended)":
' a stopped `proveo run` exits 143 (SIGTERM) or 129 (SIGHUP), not 0, and the
' pane's `echo $? > <run>.exit` records it (runner.go:548). Before, a stop read
' as a failed run and the sandbox was "kept for diagnosis"
' (_spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml).
' WHAT THE SCHEDULER RECORDS (MEASURED):
'   budget or report stop → "budget" / "done": the watcher decides those before
'     stopAgent runs, so a 143 in .exit does not change them.
'   EXTERNAL stop before the budget (someone SIGTERMs proveo) → endedEarly
'     reads 143 from .exit → "failed", which Result.Failed() makes retryable:
'     `proveo schedule` offers it and `proveo schedule retry` accepts it.
'     Under the earlier exit-0 revision the same stop recorded "ended".
'   The detail of that outside stop reads "the agent exited 143 before the
'     budget" (exitedDetail, MEASURED): it blames the agent. The transcript's
'     "outcome: stopped by SIGTERM" line tells the two apart.
' The ladder's SIGHUP (kill-session after termGrace = 1 min, runner.go:37)
' does not cut a long teardown short: proveo swallows later SIGTERM/SIGHUP once
' the first arrives, and only SIGKILL interrupts it.
' RESIDUAL (recorded, not fixed): teardown's snapshot, SaveState and `sbx rm`
' carry no timeout (MEASURED), so a HUNG proveo outlives the kill-session, and
' its late `rm` can remove a same-named sandbox the next scheduled run has
' reattached to. A per-name lock or a teardown deadline would close it
' (_spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml, residuals).
' [Unverified] against a live sbx client; unit tests pin the signal path
' (stop_signal_test.go), the stop outcome
' (TestAForwardedStopTearsDownLikeANormalExitAndReportsTheSignal, moved to
' teardown_end_test.go), the exit code
' (TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals) and the ladder, not sbx's
' response to SIGTERM.
' There is no budget cap: any positive duration is accepted.
'
' ── CLOCK + WRAP-UP (2026-10-06) ───────────────────────────────────────────
' muse-waivers ran 60 min, never wrote report.md, and was killed mid-save: the
' agent had no clock, only the prompt's "about 50 minutes", and spent 38 min
' before it read a single projection. The stop time is a fact the watcher owns:
'   typed     instruction + " Clock: proveo stops this session at <HH:MM tz>
'             (<budget> budget); write the report by <HH:MM tz>. Run `date`
'             to check."  stop = typing time + budget (≤ acceptWait earlier
'             than the real stop: errs early); times in the job's tz
'   wrap-up   lead = min(wrapUpBefore 10 m, budget/4), skipped below wrapUpMin
'             (1 m: a 2-min budget has no room to wrap up); at stop − lead the
'             watcher types steerPrefix[target] + "proveo schedule: <N> minutes
'             left — this session stops at <HH:MM tz>. Stop the task and write
'             the report now with what you have." ⏎ · submitWait · ⏎ (a slash
'             menu may take the first ⏎, as with /goal and /exit)
'   steerPrefix {"hermes": "/steer "}: hermes delivers it after the running
'             tool call without ending the turn (manual steer, 2026-10-06).
'             A target without one, or a `command:` job, gets the clock line
'             only: typing into a busy TUI that does not queue is undefined.
' Skill `scheduled-run` tells the agent to run `date` before each step and to
' treat "proveo schedule:" as the call to write the report.
'
' ── ONE WATCHER PER SESSION (2026-10-06) ───────────────────────────────────
' `proveo schedule retry muse-waivers` at 23:04:16 launched while the 22:01
' run's watcher was still in its budget-stop ladder: the old agent had taken
' /exit at 23:04, so Launch saw no session and reused the name. The old
' watcher's awaitGone then found the NEW session alive, SIGTERMed its
' `proveo run` ("stream I/O: context canceled") and killed it; both results
' finished at 23:06:34, 0.11 s apart.
' Names are reused, and so are tmux session ids: once the last session ends
' the server exits and the next one restarts at $0 (probe, tmux 3.7b). The
' pane's pid is not reused within minutes, so:
'   Pin       watch reads #{pane_pid} when it starts and pins the Session to it
'   Alive     has-session ∧ (unpinned ∨ #{pane_pid} = pinned pid)
'   stopAgent returns "<why>; the agent had already exited" when the pinned
'             session is gone before the first key, and sends nothing
' So a watcher only ever reads, types into or kills the session it launched with.
' covers: internal/tmux/tmux.go (Pin, Alive)
'
' ── ATTACH ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   proveo attach [task] [-r|--read-only]
'   proveo schedule attach [task] [-r|--read-only]
'   no task, terminal    picker of jobs whose tmux session is up; the choice
'                        attaches. Empty list prints "● nothing running" on
'                        stderr (stdout stays empty), and so does a host with
'                        no schedule.yml (exit 0)
'   no task, pipe        print the running tasks and stop: one Facts block
'                        keyed by task, valued with THE RUNNING VALUE above,
'                        on stdout; then ONE dim how-to on stderr, "`proveo
'                        attach <task>` opens one" (NO TTY: the picker's
'                        question could not be asked)
'   picker closed        "⚠ attach — no task selected", exit 1, Reported
'                        (R3's QUIT: the operator's choice; the run and
'                        harness pickers still end on main's ×)
'   named task           the rows below
' The schedule listing names no attach command; `proveo schedule --help` does.
' TMUX DECIDES, schedule.yml ONLY WORDS A REFUSAL (R4 critique must-fix 1): a
' session that is up attaches though its job left schedule.yml mid-run or the
' file is gone. A session that is not up is ONE × (R4, no heading):
'   × <task> — not running              dim "no tmux session proveo-sched-<task>"
'   × <task> — no such job              dim "jobs: …" (the schedule's refusal)
'   × ~/.proveo/schedule.yml — not found  dim "`proveo schedule --help` shows
'                                       its format"
'   "`proveo schedule` shows its last run" moved to attach's --help.
' Before tmux runs: `tmux attach` with no terminal on stdin is "× <task> —
' not attached", dim "tmux needs a terminal" (switch-client needs none).
' A hand-off tmux ends non-zero closes on "⚠ attach — stopped at tmux", exit
' 1, under tmux's own words (R3 HAND-OFF FAILURE), from attach and from the
' run and harness pickers alike. A clean detach prints nothing: tmux says
' "[detached …]" itself.
'   plain terminal       tmux attach [-r] -t proveo-sched-<job>
'   inside tmux          switch-client -t …  (tmux refuses a nested attach)
'   inside tmux + -r     TMUX= tmux attach -r -t …  — a nested client, detach
'                        with prefix prefix d. `switch-client -r` TOGGLES
'                        read-only on the operator's own client, which then
'                        stays read-only after switching back (tmux 3.7b man).
'                        Before tmux takes the terminal it prints ONE host
'                        item, "● tmux — nested read-only client", dim "the
'                        prefix twice, then d, detaches" (the operator, R4
'                        ATTACH NESTED: an exception to the HOW-TO rule
'                        beside R2's "Ctrl+C again leaves now")
' KNOWN, NOT FIXED: with no tmux on PATH, has-session fails, so a named task
' reads "not running" (true: the scheduler starts nothing without tmux).
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/running_test.go: TestAttachPrintsRunningTasks,
' TestAttachWithNothingRunningSaysSoOnStderr,
' TestAttachToATaskThatIsNotRunningSaysWhichWayItIsNot,
' TestAttachToARunningSessionScheduleYmlLacksStillAttaches,
' TestAFailedTmuxHandOffEndsOnStoppedAndNoCross,
' TestAttachWithoutATerminalRefusesBeforeTmux,
' TestReadOnlyAttachInsideTmuxNamesTheKeysThatLeave,
' TestClosingTheAttachPickerIsAWarningAndExitsOne.
' Sessions the launchd tick starts share the default socket
' (/private/tmp/tmux-<uid>/default), so attach reaches them.
' A writable attach sends keys to the agent; during the settle/type window
' they interleave with the watcher's instruction.
'
' ── `proveo run` FOR UNATTENDED USE ────────────────────────────────────────
'   --yes           seed from the choice cache, never draw the form
'   --addon <name>  host-chrome · browser · android; refused unless the
'                   harness offers it; the cache never overrides a flagged set
'
' ── TUI ONLY (2026-10-25) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' covers: internal/run/choices.go (scheduled, tuiForSchedule), internal/run/run.go (promptChoices)
' tmux hands `proveo run` a pty, so cacheApplies() is true and seedFromCache
' loads the operator's last interactive add-ons. A saved `desktop` (hermes,
' _spec/_plans/hermes-desktop-over-ssh.puml) would then call EnsureDesktop
' (an install prompt nobody answers) and holdForDesktop: the pane never shows
' the ready marker, so the run ends not-ready. Under PROVEO_SCHEDULE:
'   cached desktop  -> dropped AFTER Remember, so the saved choice survives
'   --addon desktop -> refused (the job's addons name it)
'
' ── DESCRIBE: `proveo schedule run <task> --print` (2026-10-25) ─────────────
' covers: internal/schedule/runner.go (Describe), cmd/proveo/schedule.go (printScheduledRun)
' covers: internal/sbx/kitv3.go (Launched), internal/run/run.go (print mode)
' Executor asked for the exact chain a job runs. It prints, in order:
'   # session      the `sh -c` line tmux starts (sessionCommand, <stamp> for the
'                  transcript); a `command:` job stops here
'   # sandbox      `proveo run --print <target> …` in the job's workdir with
'   # agent        PROVEO_SCHEDULE=1: sbx create, sbx run
'   # in-sandbox   sbx.Launched: ENTRYPOINT[0] + trailing command, else
'                  ENTRYPOINT + CMD (MEASURED P7, sbx-kit-v3-migration.puml);
'                  the def entrypoint then execs its agent with its launch args
'   # typed        Instruction + Clock as if the agent were ready now
' Print mode skips the choice cache, but a scheduled run applies it (pty), so
' under PROVEO_SCHEDULE the print seeds from the cache too; it never saves.
'
' ── E2E, NO MODEL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A `command:` job stands in for the agent: it prints FAKE-READY>, reads one
' line, echoes it. The test pins PROVEO_SCHEDULE_NOW, runs a real tick, and
' asserts only WHEN it fired ("due 2026-09-27T11:35:00-04:00") and WHAT it typed
' ("/goal <prompt>"). First run caught a nil tmux runner in Launch.
'
' ── INSTALL, UNINSTALL, THE TICK'S STATE (2026-11-11, R4) ──────────────────
' Install, Uninstall and TickStatus take a schedule.Runner (launchctl and
' systemctl's argv in, combined output back); cmd/proveo passes
' serviceManager, schedule.ExecRunner unless a test replaced it. A Runner
' keeps a test off the host's service manager but NOT off its files: the
' plist and unit paths come from os.UserHomeDir, so every Install or
' Uninstall test sets HOME to a temp dir (no t.Parallel) and checks the
' operator's own tick files kept their state (install_test.go testsHome).
'   install    "✓ tick — installed", the manager and "logs to <~log>" dim;
'              "⚠ tick — reads ~/.proveo/schedule.yml, not this home's" in its
'              place under another PROVEO_HOME; "× tick — no service manager
'              on <os>" (ErrNoServiceManager), its manual tick dim off windows
'   uninstall  "✓ tick — removed" when launchd or systemd let one go or a unit
'              file was there (a job launchd held with its plist gone counts);
'              "● tick — not installed" otherwise, every OS
' TickStatus reads `launchctl print`: "last exit code" (0 and "(never
' exited)" are healthy) and "stdout path", the log the tick really writes.
' KNOWN, NOT FIXED (the operator, "no false ✓; record fix"): the plist and the
' unit set PATH only, so the tick reads $HOME/.proveo whatever PROVEO_HOME the
' operator set (README's PROVEO_HOME override); the listing names it as ⚠
' instead of ✓. The fix is for the plist and the unit to carry PROVEO_HOME;
' then Tick.Home reads it from them.
' KNOWN: a job removed from schedule.yml while its session runs is invisible
' to the listing and to attach's no-argument list (both iterate the
' configured jobs); `proveo attach <task>` still opens it (tmux decides).
'
' ── LIMITS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A sleeping Mac runs nothing (waking needs `pmset`, i.e. sudo). The watcher
' does not re-prompt a stalled agent; `/goal`'s judge continues after each turn.

rectangle "launchd / systemd\nevery 60 s" as T
component "proveo schedule tick\nstateless" as TICK
component "tmux proveo-sched-<job>\nproveo run --yes --addon …" as S
component "proveo schedule watch\ncaffeinate · type /goal · budget" as W
folder "~/.proveo/logs/schedule/<job>\n<stamp>.log + .json" as L

T --> TICK
TICK --> S : Launch
TICK --> W : setsid
W --> S : WaitFor ready · send-keys
S --> L : pipe-pane
W --> L : result

note right of W
  **Typed, not passed.** `/goal` only
  works as input to the running TUI,
  so the watcher types it once the
  ready marker is on screen.
end note
@enduml
